# Story 2: Installing Rysh (45s)
# Hook: One command to install. macOS, Linux, Windows, or straight from source.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-002-installing-rysh.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
One command to install -- on every platform Rysh supports.

[00:04.0 --> 00:12.0]
On macOS, tap the repo and brew install rysh. Two commands and you're done.

[00:12.0 --> 00:20.0]
On Debian or Ubuntu, apt install rysh. On Fedora or RHEL, dnf install rysh.

[00:20.0 --> 00:27.0]
On Windows, install with WinGet.

[00:27.0 --> 00:36.0]
Or build from source -- it's just Go. make build, then make install.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
Verify it with rysh --version. You're ready to go.

